venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
# The raw parquet cache stays out of git (it lives on a GitHub Release, see
# scripts/fetch_cache.py). Odds snapshots and derived tables are tracked:
# they are small, and their commit history is the audit trail.
/data/*
!/data/odds/
!/data/derived/
# ...except the run log, which is the one thing in there that is output rather
# than data. `dashboard/scripts/daily.sh:15` points it at data/odds/, inside the
# re-included directory, and `lines.yml` stages that directory unconditionally
# (`git add data/odds`). So on any commit made from a checkout that has run the
# daily script, this file goes with it. It carries absolute paths from whichever
# machine wrote it, which on this one means a username and the repo's old
# directory name, published to a repo whose whole point is being public.
/data/odds/*.log

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.vscode/*.json

# generated output
*.egg-info/
nfl_data_profile.html
data_handling/explorer/cache/

# secrets
.env

# dashboard frontend
dashboard/web/node_modules/
dashboard/web/dist/
